    "detailed_description": "It was the year 58 B.C.<br><br>In this year, a new governor arrived in Gaul.<br>He was the Consul of the previous year and a renowned figure in the winds of Roman politics.<br><br>His name was Gaius Julius Caesar.<br><br>With great ambition in his heart, Caesar came to this land.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Simple command system</h2>A simple command system with one command per turn.<br>The simple rules make it easy to play.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Chapter-based campaign structure</h2>The story progresses by achieving chapter goals.<br>The game is over if the goal is not achieved, so the game progresses without getting dull.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Various sub-stories</h2>A variety of sub-stories are told by each tribe.<br>Early on, stories about Helvetii and Sequani unfold.<br>Later on, stories about the Germani and Britanni, who are powerful enemies, will also unfold.<br>Each time you play, the story will unfold differently.",
